      "content": "Wait, I think I lost you there. You mentioned a \"goblin\" trying to push a boulder—I don't follow. Can you please stick to the technical mechanics? \n\nYou were talking about the line pressure control solenoid valve and the shift solenoids. Can you explain exactly how a worn valve spool causes a pressure surge during those specific upshifts (3-4 and 5-6) without the solenoid duty cycle showing an error? I need the actual mechanical interaction between the spool and the hydraulic circuit.",
